# This repo is static HTML served by GitHub Pages. There is no build system — no Gradle, no
# npm, no bundler — so it produces no build output, no dependency directory and no compiled
# artefact, and this file deliberately names none of those.
#
# That omission is the point. The 2026-09-04 S6 audit brought six repos to a credential
# baseline; copying an Android baseline in here would have listed *.jks, build/, .gradle/,
# local.properties and thirty more patterns for files this repo cannot produce. A .gitignore
# that names things a repo cannot produce is noise, and noise is what stops people reading it —
# the same failure as a check nobody looks at any more.
#
# What is listed below is only what can actually appear in a directory somebody edits HTML in.

# Editor and OS droppings — these WILL appear
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
*.orig
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# The two credential shapes that can plausibly reach a repo with no build. Neither is used
# here and neither has ever appeared; they are listed because the audit's finding was that a
# protection list written from a repo's own incidents protects only against its past.
# The real PAT lives at C:\Projects\.github_pat, outside every repo.
.env
.github_pat
